  "scope": [
    "Run one bounded live process-only comparison of Routed Context versus Full-load Context using the same approved model and reasoning effort across matched task shapes.",
    "Freeze assignment order, cache-control rule, acquisition classification, quality rubric, Provider contract, privacy boundary, operational Token ceiling, wall-clock ceiling, zero retry, and zero fallback before generation.",
    "Complete generation-free preparation and stop for exact protocol approval before any model invocation; then retain objective quality, Token components, latency, acquisition, and cache-sensitivity evidence for an evidence-bounded conclusion."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "A content-addressed protocol and approval template isolate context treatment as the causal factor and keep model, reasoning, repository revision, tasks, tooling, and evaluator fixed.",
    "Preflight proves every candidate package, fixture, command boundary, output schema, cache-control requirement, stop condition, and Provider field against the installed contract without generating model output.",
    "The live run cannot start without an affirmative approval matching the exact protocol digest, model, reasoning effort, sample count, Token ceiling, time ceiling, and Pro-only spending boundary.",
    "Analysis makes objective quality primary, reports gross input, cached input, non-cached input, output, Operational Tokens, latency, human intervention, rework, and acquisition coverage separately, and blocks causal claims when cache control fails.",
    "No retry, fallback, automatic routing change, historical evidence rewrite, external publication, or production action occurs."
  ],
